    "lawCode": "Add §104, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5868A\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to facilitating\naccess to telephone providers to deliver fiber-based services\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nFacilitates access to telephone providers to deliver fiber-based.\nservices.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends public service law to create new section 104.\n\nSection 2. Provides compensation to property owner under section 228 of\nthe public service law. It also allows a telephone provider to replace\nexisting facilities placed previously by a telephone corporation in a\nbuilding with fiber optic facilities for purposes of providing any tele-\nphone, broadband, cable or other video service that the telephone corpo-\nration needs to service consumers.\n\nSection 3. Provides requirements that telephone or tenant or combination\nof, bear the entire cost of theòinstallation, operation or removal of\nsuch facilities; or that the telephone corporation agrees to indemnify\nthe landlord or property owner for any damage caused by the installa-\ntion, operation or removal of facilities.\n\nSection 2. States the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThere are instances where a consumer can't secure broadband from a\nprovider because the building owner in which they live or a nearby\nbuilding/property owner blocks broadband providers from gaining access\nto a location in order to deliver broadband services. In New York City\nalone, there are over 160,000 properties that providers can't access.\nThis legislation would help address this problem, assist in bridging the\ndigital divide, and promote competition.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021/22: S5868 - REFERRED TO ENERGY AND TELECOMMUNICATIONS\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the sixtieth day after it shall have\nbecome law.\n",
